## Context
Prose review panel 2026-06-11 (pre-arXiv): two reviewers reached major-revision
on claim strength, convergent on three findings. These are author-judgment
rewrites of abstract and conclusion — not mechanical.

1. **Headline claim outruns evidence.** "The binding constraint is the data,
   not the model" rests on the unregistered exploratory documents condition,
   N=4 agents, single-query only — and the paper itself notes multi-turn does
   not equalise (Anthropic 0.61→0.38). Reframe as hypothesis; carry k/n
   directional hedging into abstract and conclusion.
2. **ρ=0.92 in the abstract without the across-model-confound caveat.** The
   honest within-model signal is the modest stratified τ (+0.215, positive in
   10/14 models); only 3/14 models contribute to the binary gap. Abstract must
   carry the "pooled, in-sample existence proof" qualification.
3. **"Falls short of the four-dimensional quality bar" with two dimensions
   measured.** Coherence/provenance/temporality rubric deferred to Phase C;
   scope the claim to measured dimensions.

Suggestion from same review: abstract ~400 words, omits best number
(fusion F1=0.813); consider adding the seeding-mechanism clause and trimming.

Sequencing: runs AFTER sibling 0533 (factual fixes in the body, including
seeding attribution and the seeded-recall built-fleet scope). The rewrite sits
on top of those corrections — keep abstract/conclusion seeded-recall language
scoped to the built fleet, consistent with whatever attribution 0533 lands.

The defect sites are abstract (line ~31) and conclusion (line ~202) ONLY.
§Exp2 body (line ~148, "relocates the binding constraint ... unregistered and
exploratory ... four-agent cohort") and Discussion (line ~182, "existence
proof rather than a validated detector") are already correctly hedged — the
abstract/conclusion must be brought to THEIR register; do not edit them.

## Relevant files
- `slides/manuscript/main.md` — abstract (l.~31), conclusion (l.~202);
  reference register at §Exp2 l.~148, Discussion l.~182, annex-screen l.~513–523

## Actions
1. Abstract: reframe the binding-constraint opener as a directional
   hypothesis with k/n hedging (3/4 agents equalise in single-query; multi-turn
   does not replicate).
2. Abstract: scope the seeded-recall ceiling sentence to the built fleet
   ("Wikipedia covers 92% of the built fleet ..."), consistent with 0533.
3. Abstract: scope the quality-bar sentence to the measured dimensions
   (accuracy/F1, coverage, citation-based provenance), naming the deferred
   rubric (coherence, provenance support, temporality) as follow-on work.
4. Abstract: harden the ρ=0.92 caveat — explicitly name the across-model
   confound; within-model signal is stratified τ=+0.215, 10/14 models;
   match the Discussion's "existence proof" register.
5. Abstract: OPTIONAL (author decision, mark clearly in PR body): add the
   fusion result (majority vote of 2-of-4 agents → F1=0.813, 122 plants,
   5 false positives) and trim ~30–50 words elsewhere to compensate.
6. Conclusion: same hypothesis reframing as Action 1 ("the evidence points
   toward a conjecture: ... bottleneck relocates from model capability to
   document quality — observed in single-query across three of four agents,
   not replicated multi-turn").
7. Conclusion: same quality-bar scoping as Action 3.
8. Conclusion: seeded-recall sentence already carries "92% of the built
   fleet" — verify consistency with 0533's landed attribution wording; minor
   cleanup only.

Keep diffs surgical; preserve the author's voice; no edits outside abstract
and conclusion. Do not introduce a macro for τ (appears twice; inline it).

## Test
- Re-run prose review panel post-rewrite: methods + adversarial reviewers no
  longer major on claim strength.

## Exit criteria
- [ ] Headline data-vs-model claim reframed as hypothesis with explicit scope.
- [ ] ρ=0.92 carries the pooled/confound caveat wherever it appears.
- [ ] Quality-bar claim scoped to the two measured dimensions.
- [ ] Author has read and blessed the rewritten abstract + conclusion.

## Author annotation brief (reading 1, 2026-06-11) — this unblocks the needs-human items

Abstract rewrite directives (author, from main+hdm.pdf p1–2):
- "177 thermal power plants" must not read as 177 *operating* plants — the
  register spans proposed/planned/abandoned/retired too. Disambiguate.
- The long benchmark-results sentence loses the general reader — simplify.
- "Four frontier agents … four-dimensional quality bar": confusing reuse of
  "four"; rephrase one of them.
- Remove F1 detail from the abstract ("only you are in love with F1").
- Remove the ρ=0.92 screening sentence as too complicated (will be superseded
  by the 0505-line raid results); keep at most a plain-language claim.
- No literature review in the abstract (drop the "to our knowledge no prior
  benchmark" closing); remove the fusion/pooling sentence — stay focused.
- Em-dashes are an AI tell — restyle.
- Key results, restated by the author (use as the abstract's spine and in the
  intro): (1) we offer a new computable benchmark; (2) the task is hard for
  today's agents; (3) reference-free coherence criteria suffice to screen out
  the weak models.
- Intro: consider reintegrating the key-results list before the outline
  announcement. We do NOT check/trace per-cell provenance — instead add a
  sentence contextualising computable benchmarks in knowledge engineering & AI.
- Conclusion (p23): currently weakly supported by results — argue better.
